WEBVTT

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:10.010
"The Battle of Hangu Pass, Day 16"

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:18.510
"Han" "Zhao" "Chu" "Wei" "Yan"

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:25.020
The Chu general has arrived!

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.570
You're late, Wa Lin.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:31.280
Whoops. Sorry.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.610
Just one of those mornings.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:37.070
This must be their second general, Wa Lin.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:37.990
"Acting Commanding General of Han -
Zhang Yin"

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:37.990
This must be their second general, Wa Lin.

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.950
"Acting Commanding General of Han -
Zhang Yin"

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.950
Sh-She's huge...

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:43.830
So? Who was it?

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:46.460
Which one of you morons
got duped by Wang Jian?

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:47.290
Mor--

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:49.250
If not for his screw-up,

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:54.090
we would all be waltzing
through Hangu Pass by now.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:55.220
Was it you?

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:59.390
Er, n-no... I'm Zhang Yin of Han.

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:01.100
Hey, giantess.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:04.310
Did you just call the
great Wu Lu Duo a moron?

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:06.480
Oh, so <i>you're </i>the moron.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.860
What was that? "Giantess"?

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:12.610
Enough, Wa Lin. That discussion is over.

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:15.200
Well, <i>I </i>didn't hear any of it.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:19.370
Still, "giantess" is an awful thing
to call a young maiden.

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:21.660
Isn't it, Zhang Yin of Han?

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:24.120
Um, I, er, that is...

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.910
Listen up, Yan.

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:30.590
No one's called me "giantess" and lived.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.340
Now what, hmm?

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:36.630
What, are you sensitive about your height?

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:38.510
I find it rather arousing.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:41.510
If you like, I can sleep with you tonight.

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:44.310
My, what a treat.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:45.560
Wa Lin!

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.310
That's quite enough!

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.520
Do you understand
the gravity of the situation?

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:57.240
The predicament we face could well mean
the coalition army ending in failure.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.240
To return empty-handed after
plotting such an ambitious war,

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:05.620
without breaching Hangu Pass,
much less storming Xianyang,

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:08.170
will make us the world's laughingstocks!

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:12.250
How dare you show your faces back home?

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:19.180
Since you bring it up...

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:21.430
The ones who most stand to lose face

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:26.730
are Lord Chunshen, self-proclaimed
leader of the coalition army,

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:30.230
and Li Mu, who was
pulling all the strings.

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:32.190
Though he seems to be running late.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:35.480
Oh? Li Mu's not here yet?

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:39.780
Don't tell me he's in bed, depressed.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:45.450
Li Mu has already left the coalition army.

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:47.160
H-He <i>what</i>?!

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:52.080
"Select a thousand of the best
troops from each nation's army

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.340
and send them to Li Mu."

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.340
That's the command he left behind.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:00.720
One thousand elite troops--to Li Mu?

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:05.260
A thousand? Not much manpower,
if he's planning something.

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:09.560
First, tell us: Where <i>is </i>Li Mu?

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.980
Hey. Zhao!

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:17.030
Did you know all of this
from the very beginning?

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:18.690
Yes.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.400
Damn that Li Mu.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.870
Huh...

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:58.460
"Li Mu's Whereabouts"

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:04.420
Guess it's just a
staring contest today, eh?

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:07.590
They're fresh out of ways to attack.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:23.070
And so days 16 and 17 came to an end.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:26.030
"Atop the Palace Court Wall, Xianyang"

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:26.030
And so days 16 and 17 came to an end.

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:33.870
"The Small City of Huasha
in the Xianyang Mountains"

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:36.290
Word is the coalition army'll
be leavin' soon.

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:36.830
"Qin"

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:39.840
"Qin"

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:39.840
You think General Meng Wu
got that first big win?

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:43.010
'Course he did! He beat Chu, didn't he?

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:47.590
Yeah, but what's this about
General Wang Jian saving Hangu Pass?

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:52.890
Hey, what the--

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:55.520
What's <i>that</i>?

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:58.020
We should be wary of the Yan army.

00:05:58.020 --> 00:05:59.860
They still have plenty of muscle!

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:03.070
Let Wang Jian handle them.

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:05.150
--High Commander!
--What is it?

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:08.860
We've received word that a tiny castle
named Huasha is under enemy attack!

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:09.910
What?

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:13.240
Huasha? Where is this castle?

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:16.660
Bring us a second map!

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:20.040
It's outside the mountains
that surround Xianyang.

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:26.300
An odd place to be under attack.

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:29.760
It's on this side of
our southern gate at Wu Pass.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:32.300
Is this some kind of mistake?

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:38.480
Hangu Pass is not the only path
the foe may take to reach Xianyang.

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:41.520
Just as the northern road
enters through Hangu Pass,

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:44.150
this southern road goes through Wu Pass.

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:45.900
High Commander!

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:50.110
Smoke signals indicate that the small
castles of Zong and Luan have fallen!

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:54.200
"Luan" "Zong" "Huasha"

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:56.160
They're getting closer--

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:58.500
closer to Xianyang!

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:01.290
Has the enemy invaded
by the southern road?

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:04.380
No--ridiculous. That's inconceivable.

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:09.970
There's not even any fighting
at our southern gate of Wu Pass!

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:13.850
Beyond Luan lies
the central city of Neifu.

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:17.430
Jie Yi, go to Neifu and
get a read on the situation.

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:19.350
Take a thousand troops with you.

00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:20.310
Yes, sir!

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:22.020
Urgent report!

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:23.360
Neifu is under attack!

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:26.980
The neighboring castle of Renmi
is requesting reinforcements!

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:30.490
Renmi hereby asks Xianyang to send troops!

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:36.370
The... The foe's reached Neifu, too?

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:39.000
What on earth is happening?

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:43.500
"Neifu"

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:47.800
Neifu has fallen--and at last
we know who's attacking!

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:51.550
It appears the man
leading the enemy army...

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:53.300
...is Li Mu!

00:07:56.260 --> 00:08:00.270
"Renmi"

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:04.770
It's no use! There are too many of them!

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:07.440
The rear guard will suffice for the rest.

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:09.440
Hurry the main forces onward.

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:11.950
Sir!

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:14.240
As the enemy continues its
assault on Renmi,

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:15.990
they've crossed Qin's midpoint!

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:19.040
They're coming by the southern road,
Xianyang in their sights!

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:20.660
Li Mu...

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:23.500
They number from 30 to 40 thousand!

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:25.960
N-Nearly 40 thousand?!

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:28.250
But they didn't enter by Wu Pass--

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:31.590
how could Li Mu get so many
troops on the southern road?

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:35.010
The fact of the matter is
that Wu Pass was not breached.

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:37.300
Which means they must have
entered from the mountains,

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:40.520
midway along the southern road.

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:46.020
But it would take several days
to move an army of that size--

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:49.650
Was Li Mu planning this all along?

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:53.570
Surely this is no time
to leisurely dissect his tricks.

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:57.570
Li Mu is nearly upon us as we speak.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:59.450
Exactly right.

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:04.500
If he's already past Renmi,
he's practically under our very noses.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:09.000
We must act in all haste--or
be swallowed up where we stand.

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:14.630
Which means...

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:16.470
Here we go--

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:19.640
the royal capital Xianyang, a battlefield!

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:21.560
Can we defend it?

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:26.140
With half of Xianyang's
troops at Hangu Pass,

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:28.310
it is the very definition of shorthanded.

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:32.860
Worse, Xianyang has never
experienced an enemy onslaught.

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:36.320
In that sense, too,
it is hardly a strong castle.

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:40.240
Yet with the coalition army
keeping a close eye on us,

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:43.660
we can't call our troops back
from Hangu Pass.

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:47.830
Only two options remain:

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:51.210
Set out down the
southern road to defeat Li Mu

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:54.340
or guard Xianyang with the troops at hand.

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:59.800
But this castle lacks the capacity
to stop Li Mu's army.

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:02.470
So we can only set out to meet him.

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:08.520
We'll have to carefully run
multiple simulations, of course.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:11.900
There's no time.
Lord Changwen, your assistance?

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:13.610
Y-Yes.

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:17.490
Bring in the troop
and cavalry pieces, quickly!

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:21.950
Can one even <i>run </i>simulation
battles against Li Mu?

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:24.910
Good heavens...

00:10:26.410 --> 00:10:31.670
Things certainly have
gotten grim, haven't they?

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:34.840
"Chu"

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:42.850
He's one hell of a man, all right,

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:44.470
that Li Mu.

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:50.480
Sending ten thousand troops
down that southern road?

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:54.320
It'll take days to cross those mountains.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.740
He's been sending Zhao troops that way

00:10:56.740 --> 00:11:01.200
ever since the war
began--thousands at a time--

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:03.740
so no one would notice.

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:11.250
But didn't the enemy notice that
40 thousand of our troops went missing?

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:13.250
They wouldn't.

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:18.130
That battle started out with
200 thousand versus 40 thousand.

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:22.340
That's twice the number of
foes you can estimate by feel.

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:26.890
B-But if Li Mu's been
sending troops since the war began,

00:11:26.890 --> 00:11:30.600
doesn't that mean he'd already
given up on us after Lord Linwu's blunder

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:32.980
on the very first day?

00:11:34.610 --> 00:11:36.610
Nope!

00:11:36.610 --> 00:11:40.860
Recall the Zhao army's position
in the Battle of Hangu Pass.

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:42.870
They were closest to the southern road--

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:47.660
perfect for sending troops
without anyone noticing.

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:49.710
And that's why they were there!

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:55.340
Li Mu had been working on a detached force
even before this war began!

00:11:55.340 --> 00:11:57.210
M-My goodness!

00:11:57.210 --> 00:11:59.760
His every move has a reason!

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:01.090
Die!

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:04.850
Eeeyikes!

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:10.020
We think alike, the two of us.

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:13.270
Where we differ is in
our consideration of others.

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:15.190
Consideration, you say?

00:12:15.190 --> 00:12:19.820
In that he summoned a thousand
elite troops from each army, I mean.

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:24.450
They'll never make it
in time--not at this stage.

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:31.750
Later he can tell the other nations that
the credit doesn't belong to Zhao alone.

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:34.710
Tch! That Li Mu is too good to be true!

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:38.750
Infuriating as it is to admit,
if he's that perfect...

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:43.590
Why, if he came to me
with a sweet look on his face,

00:12:43.590 --> 00:12:46.760
I might not mind giving him my chastity.

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:50.600
Oh.

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:53.100
The next targets after Renmi would be...

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:56.020
Shi and Lang, is it?

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:58.770
They're so small--they won't last long!

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:03.200
No: Shi in the lowlands
and Lang in the highlands

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:05.740
work together as a defensive outpost.

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:08.830
They ought to be able to buy us some time.

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:14.580
Here they come!

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:17.330
The enemy! Enemy attack!

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:19.130
Where are they?!

00:13:19.130 --> 00:13:20.750
Up above!

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:22.590
<i>Above?!</i>

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:24.090
N-No way!

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:27.180
Horses? On a cliff like that?!

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:33.770
That Kaine's as fast as ever!

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:35.940
Follow her!

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:37.860
Ur-Urgent report!

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:39.980
Shi and Lang have both fallen!

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:41.860
Repeat: They have fallen!

00:13:41.860 --> 00:13:44.240
They <i>what</i>?!

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:47.820
That's absurd--it happened so fast!

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:50.120
Is Li Mu some kind of monster?

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:55.080
This is bad.

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:59.250
They haven't even left us
enough time to hash out a strategy.

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:07.380
Li Mu, sir.

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:09.970
The troops' pace grows ever more sluggish.

00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:12.140
May we rest a while and regroup?

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:16.100
No. We continue onward at this same speed.

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:19.150
Tell Kaine and the others up
ahead to do the same.

00:14:19.150 --> 00:14:20.980
Sir!

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:24.320
It's now but a two-day
journey to Xianyang.

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:29.200
We must arrive as quickly
as possible to stay their hand.

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:47.170
We're under attack!

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:54.100
All troops, halt! The enemy's
approaching from behind!

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:56.810
Li Mu, sir--is that--

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:58.440
Lord Biao.

00:15:05.440 --> 00:15:06.400
What?

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:10.860
Are you saying our army
attacked Li Mu's from behind?!

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:14.700
Yes! Th-The intel is still unconfirmed,

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:17.660
but per our scout's report,
that army's flags...

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:19.540
"Biao"

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:21.380
...bore the character "Biao"!

00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:22.330
"Biao"?!

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:24.130
Lord Biao's army?

00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:25.920
And separately...

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:27.420
"Fei"

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:29.800
"Fei"

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:29.800
...there were those that read "Fei"!

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:33.930
The Fei Xin Force!

00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:37.180
Xin... so you're there, too?

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:41.980
That ought to buy us a bit more time.

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:45.360
But I find it all just
a touch too miraculous.

00:15:45.360 --> 00:15:48.940
It makes me doubt
the accuracy of the report.

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:52.910
Lord Biao's army <i>should </i>be
fighting at Hangu Pass.

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:57.740
How, then, can it simply
appear on the southern road?

00:15:57.740 --> 00:15:59.830
He's right.

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:03.290
What in blazes is going on out there?

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:07.340
"Four Days Earlier
(The 16th Day of Battle)"

00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:10.720
It did not escape Lord Biao's attention.

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:15.970
The thousand-man units selected
from each coalition army member

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:20.310
sent up the tiniest dust clouds
as they made their way to Li Mu.

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:24.730
A-Are you sure we can just up and leave?

00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:25.900
And 3 thousand of us, too!

00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:29.360
"The real battle
might not be at Hangu Pass"?

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:31.240
What does that even <i>mean</i>?

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:33.410
It's just a general's intuition.

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:35.820
If he's wrong, there'll be hell to pay.

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:36.660
Huh?

00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:39.870
But if he's right, this will be
the worst-case scenario.

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:40.830
Wha--

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:44.250
I mean, even our captain...

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:46.630
I get that you're hesitatin'.

00:16:46.630 --> 00:16:49.670
But I had my suspicions, too.

00:16:49.670 --> 00:16:53.300
That's why I decided
to tag along after Lord Biao.

00:16:58.100 --> 00:17:00.020
No doubt about it--

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:01.730
that's the Li Mu Army!

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:04.440
L-Look!

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:07.520
Lord Biao's might is unstoppable!

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:09.650
"Li"

00:17:09.650 --> 00:17:13.900
"Li"

00:17:09.650 --> 00:17:13.900
What are you doing? All troops,
redeploy in formation facing the rear!

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:17.450
Li Mu, sir, let the main forces
escape to the front.

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:19.540
We'll recall the elite cavalry there

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:22.080
and bolster our offenses--just in case.

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:23.290
No.

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:26.630
There's no need to recall
Kaine and the others.

00:17:26.630 --> 00:17:29.590
We'll handle this right here.

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:31.090
Use the Liudong flow!

00:17:31.090 --> 00:17:34.840
Bei Zhen, Bei Li, Guan Lie:
to your pivot positions!

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:36.130
Sir!

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:39.260
Do <i>not </i>miss any of my signals.

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:40.310
Sir!

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:43.390
Oh! The Li Mu Army's made a move!

00:17:43.390 --> 00:17:45.980
He means to fight!

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:49.270
Main forces, raise all your flags.

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:52.860
We'll force our way in.
Stay close together.

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:54.030
Let's go!

00:17:56.610 --> 00:17:59.070
Those flags! That's their main forces!

00:17:59.070 --> 00:18:00.370
They're on the move!

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:02.040
They're <i>running</i>¡

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:03.580
That's where Li Mu is!

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:05.370
You're not getting away, idiot!

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:08.420
Hmm? Hang on--what's with those guys?

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:09.000
"Li"

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:10.790
"Li"

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:10.790
You'd think they're
running to the outside,

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:12.960
"Li"

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:12.960
but they're moving
<i>inside</i>--on the diagonal!

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:17.470
Our surprise attack
musta scrambled their brains!

00:18:17.470 --> 00:18:22.010
They're just gonna push aside
their allies and make a huge mess!

00:18:27.020 --> 00:18:28.480
What...

00:18:28.480 --> 00:18:30.360
What on earth?

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:33.440
The battlefield's one big whirlpool...

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:35.940
Their main forces
are wedging their way in,

00:18:35.940 --> 00:18:39.110
being pushed aside,
and creating this flow.

00:18:40.200 --> 00:18:44.660
Wait--I've seen this once before.

00:18:44.660 --> 00:18:47.790
That's right: before
the Battle of Hangu Pass,

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:53.050
the Zhao army tried to set up
the same kind of maneuver.

00:18:53.050 --> 00:18:59.220
That maneuver ended
when Lord Biao halted his advance.

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:01.720
But this time...

00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:05.220
Dammit! This weird flow
is keepin' us away!

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:07.350
But I can <i>see </i>those bastards!

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:11.520
No--the flow is traveling <i>toward </i>them!

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:15.440
Don't fight it, follow it.
We'll wind up at their backs!

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:17.190
All right, let's--

00:19:19.070 --> 00:19:22.030
Watch out for the big wad of enemies here!

00:19:22.030 --> 00:19:23.910
Stay close together!

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:26.040
No need to kill anyone!

00:19:28.910 --> 00:19:30.670
Our unit!

00:19:30.670 --> 00:19:33.460
They just got split in two!

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:36.550
Damn! We're separated
from Xin and the others!

00:19:36.550 --> 00:19:38.220
We need to move left...

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:41.510
Captain! Lieutenant Yuan
is way over there!

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:43.510
What?!

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:47.270
That was too shallow a slice.
Move Guan Lie ten paces inside!

00:19:47.270 --> 00:19:48.640
Sir!

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:51.730
It's no use! We're drifting away
from Yuan and the others!

00:19:51.730 --> 00:19:53.190
Dammit!

00:19:53.190 --> 00:19:55.020
Another cluster of enemies!

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:57.320
Ah! Split up <i>again</i>!

00:19:57.320 --> 00:19:59.990
It's happening all over.

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:03.120
Here and there are spots
that go against the flow--

00:20:03.120 --> 00:20:07.700
and that's where we're splitting.

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:11.330
Leaves, following the current
on the water's surface...

00:20:11.330 --> 00:20:14.000
An immobile rock sits in the eddy,

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:17.300
sending the leaves
in different directions.

00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:22.340
And the pivotal rocks that
are splintering <i>this </i>current

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:24.640
are under Li Mu's control!

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:26.970
Stay close together!

00:20:26.970 --> 00:20:31.560
But <i>I'm </i>seeing and understanding
all this from up here.

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:37.150
Our troops down in the thick of it
will have no idea what's going on!

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:43.950
No wonder that Wei general tried out
this technique from up in a tower.

00:20:43.950 --> 00:20:49.490
Then how can Li Mu see everything
from down on the ground?

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:51.330
They can't be in there!

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:52.830
I'm off to help them!

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:55.670
The more they chase
the bait of the main forces,

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:58.750
the more powerful the whirlpool becomes!

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:01.840
We've got to get everyone
outside that eddy!

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:05.180
Dammit! Just can't get close to 'em!

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:07.890
Captain, we've been splintered again!

00:21:07.890 --> 00:21:09.260
It's no use, Xin!

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:10.100
Bi!

00:21:10.100 --> 00:21:13.770
We should remove ourselves
from this current!

00:21:13.770 --> 00:21:16.860
At this rate,
our unit will only waste away!

00:21:16.860 --> 00:21:20.030
No! I can see Li Mu and his men!

00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:22.610
We're gonna rush on in there, Bi!

00:21:22.610 --> 00:21:23.490
Xin!

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:28.490
I know what they're doin' with
this weird current and all those clumps!

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:33.040
But if we go in the right direction,
I just <i>know </i>we'll reach the main forces!

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:36.960
The right direction?!
Xin, what are you saying?

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:38.710
Words're failin' me...

00:21:38.710 --> 00:21:41.000
I can't explain it, but Lord Biao--

00:21:44.550 --> 00:21:48.600
That's how Lord Biao's
gettin' closer to those bastards!

00:21:48.600 --> 00:21:49.430
What?!

00:21:49.430 --> 00:21:51.060
Lord Biao?!

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:54.520
Lord Biao's unit is still approaching!

00:21:54.520 --> 00:21:55.890
What?!

00:21:55.890 --> 00:22:02.280
Don't tell me he's figured out
Li Mu's Liudong flow maneuver!

00:22:02.280 --> 00:22:04.780
It's no use.

00:22:04.780 --> 00:22:08.530
This simple-looking current
is actually quite complex.

00:22:08.530 --> 00:22:13.450
<i>No one </i>can see through it--apart from me,
the man who orchestrated it.

00:22:17.370 --> 00:22:20.340
It's about time to bring
this technique to an end.

00:22:21.420 --> 00:22:25.010
Have Zhao Bei's and
Zhao Fa's units move inside.

00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:27.760
They should be able to surround Lord Biao.

00:22:27.760 --> 00:22:29.300
Yes, sir!

00:22:29.300 --> 00:22:31.220
Get Lord Biao!

00:22:32.890 --> 00:22:34.850
"Biao"

00:22:38.310 --> 00:22:40.400
Lord Biao's flags--they're...

00:22:40.400 --> 00:22:43.860
They're gone!

00:22:43.860 --> 00:22:45.740
Looks like it's over.

00:22:53.080 --> 00:22:55.660
I might be the instinctive type,

00:22:55.660 --> 00:23:00.250
but I'm not above little tricks
like distancing myself from my flags!

00:23:00.250 --> 00:23:04.130
In fact, that's instinct, too!

00:23:04.130 --> 00:23:07.380
Still, that being said...

00:23:07.380 --> 00:23:11.470
That was a rather fun little
muddy stream you had there!

00:23:11.470 --> 00:23:14.470
So you're Li Mu, the great flame.

00:23:14.470 --> 00:23:18.100
You're skinnier than I expected.

00:23:18.100 --> 00:23:21.610
Now, then--I'll just be taking your head.

00:24:54.320 --> 00:24:58.740
Next on <i>Kingdom</i>:
"The Ultimate Instinctive Type."
